{"type":"text","timestamp":1788416024355,"sessionID":"ses_f9a1bca88ffeOI6XQW9XGrhSp9","part":{"id":"prt_065e6df0f001zNclXPZrOG7CTU","messageID":"msg_065e6d6a2001wN2nACQ3ikH3cU","sessionID":"ses_f9a1bca88ffeOI6XQW9XGrhSp9","type":"text","text":"\n\nFixed. The change was minimal - in the `_setup_tools` method in `agents.py`, the system now checks if a `final_answer` tool was already provided before adding the default `FinalAnswerTool`. This:\n\n1. **Maintains backward compatibility** - existing code without custom `final_answer` tools continues to work\n2. **Allows custom final_answer tools** - users can now provide their own version without it being overridden\n3. **Works across all agent types** - since CodeAgent, ToolCallingAgent, and others all inherit from MultiStepAgent\n\nAdded a test `test_custom_final_answer_tool_is_respected` to verify this behavior.","time":{"start":1788416024335,"end":1788416024352}}}
